---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import ContactForm from '../../components/ContactForm.astro';
import ProofStats from '../../components/ProofStats.astro';

const title = 'SEO Results: Anonymised Portfolio Data';
const description = 'Dated Google Search Console results from an anonymised portfolio site, with clear limits on what the figures prove and how SEO performance is measured.';

const schema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://seo-guildford.uk/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Results', item: 'https://seo-guildford.uk/case-studies/' }
    ]
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: title,
    description,
    url: 'https://seo-guildford.uk/case-studies/',
    isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'SEO Guildford', url: 'https://seo-guildford.uk/' }
  }
];
---
<Base title={title} description={description} schema={schema}>
<PageHero
    eyebrow="Measured evidence"
    crumbs={[{"label": "Results"}]}
    lead="This page shows dated first-party search data from a site in my own portfolio. The domain stays anonymous. The figures come from Google Search Console."
    glance={{"heading": "At a glance", "points": ["One portfolio site, an EV charging directory, shown by sector.", "Google clicks and impressions, month by month from May to October 2026.", "Each chart names its source, metric, period and pull date.", "One site is not a promise for every site."], "facts": [{"k": "Source", "v": "Google Search Console"}, {"k": "Period", "v": "May to October 2026"}, {"k": "Data pulled", "v": "7 November 2026"}]}}
    proof={[{"v": "Free first audit", "l": "a short PDF report by email. No payment details and no obligation.", "href": "/free-seo-audit-guildford/"}, {"v": "1 working day", "l": "to reply to every enquiry. The reply comes from me.", "href": "/contact/"}, {"v": "£400", "l": "for a one-off AI search audit. Monthly plans start at £500.", "href": "/seo-pricing-guildford/"}]}
    tools={false}
  >
    <Fragment slot="title">SEO Results from <span class="mark">Anonymised</span> Portfolio Data</Fragment>
  </PageHero>

  <article class="doc">
  <div class="prose">

    <h2>What the data shows</h2>

    <p>Search Console measures how often a site appears in Google Search and how many clicks those appearances produce. The charts show full calendar months only, with no projection of partial months, and one site is not a promise for every site.</p>

    <p>The useful signal is the direction and the measurement discipline. Technical fixes, content architecture, internal links, and crawl management can be tied to changes in impressions and clicks. Commercial outcomes still require lead and revenue tracking inside the business, so traffic growth alone is never described as revenue.</p>
  </div>
  </article>

  <ProofStats variant="full" />

  <article class="doc">
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What the data does not prove</h2>

    <p>An anonymous chart cannot prove that the same growth will occur in another sector. It does not replace a named testimonial, a client reference, or access to the underlying account. It also cannot isolate every cause because search performance changes with competition, seasonality, search demand, algorithm updates, and the site's own publishing history.</p>

    <p>That limitation is stated plainly. SEO Guildford does not publish invented clients, composite testimonials, or hypothetical revenue as completed work. A proposal should instead begin with your current evidence: Search Console queries, landing pages, index coverage, technical constraints, lead events, and commercial priorities.</p>

    <h2>How your performance would be measured</h2>

    <p>Measurement starts with a baseline before implementation. The baseline records clicks, impressions, average position, indexed pages, qualified leads, and any revenue data the business can reliably attribute. Each recommended change receives an owner, a deployment date, and a target metric.</p>

    <p>Reporting then separates leading indicators from business outcomes. Crawl recovery and improved impressions can show that Google is processing the work. Clicks and landing-page engagement show whether visibility is attracting the right audience. Enquiries, calls, booked meetings, and revenue determine whether the work is commercially worthwhile.</p>

    <h2>Start with your own evidence</h2>

    <p>A free audit provides a focused first look at technical health, query ownership, indexation, and obvious conversion gaps. The paid comprehensive review goes further with manual analysis, prioritisation, and implementation guidance. Both begin with the data available for your site rather than a generic forecast.</p>

    <div class="not-prose my-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
      <a href="/free-seo-audit-guildford/" class="cta-button">Request a free audit</a>
      <a href="/technical-seo-guildford/" class="cta-button-outline">Review technical SEO</a>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 pt-6 border-t border-border text-sm text-text-muted">
      <p>Related: <a href="/services/">SEO services for Guildford</a> | <a href="/seo-pricing-guildford/">Pricing</a> | <a href="/about/">How the consultancy works</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
  </article>

  <ContactForm eyebrow="Your baseline" heading="Measure what your site can improve" subject="SEO Guildford: Results page enquiry" />
</Base>
